      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think double `kill` is okay. It\u0027s simple and correct. Generally, we don\u0027t want to do too many things between `fork` and `exec` in a multi-threaded program because it can lead to deadlock issues [1]. Your code looks fine because you don\u0027t have things like `malloc`, `new`, and `make_unique` that either directly or indirectly touch a global lock, but this is hard to be thoroughly checked and is error-prone as the code evolves.\n\nIf you can upload a CL that uses the double `kill` approach, I\u0027m happy to take it.\n\n[1] https://www.evanjones.ca/fork-is-dangerous.html",
